{"title":"2024 IOQM Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">25</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-26\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">26</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-27\"><a href=\"#Problem_21\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">27</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 21</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-28\"><a href=\"#Problem_22\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">28</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 22</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-29\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">29</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-30\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">30</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-31\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">31</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-32\"><a href=\"#Problem_26\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">32</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 26</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-33\"><a href=\"#Problem_27\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">33</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 27</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-34\"><a href=\"#Problem_28\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">34</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 28</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-35\"><a href=\"#Problem_29\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">35</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 29</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-36\"><a href=\"#Problem_30\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">36</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 30</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest positive integer that does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd85a668b732c402b09f5456ff00c453286f314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times2\\times3\\times4\\times5\\times6\\times7\\times8\\times9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"261\" height=\"15\" /> is:\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36411d3d14ed2f340505fa664981ab0f1ece03e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdots9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are factors of the product. By commutativity,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e0c71ed23e0d1d5a18be1614497e94d1c5b06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdots9=2\\cdot5\\cdot(\\text{other factors})=10(\\text{other factors})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"415\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime, by Euclid's lemma, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36411d3d14ed2f340505fa664981ab0f1ece03e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdots9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must divide one of the factors.\n</p><p>But\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3106e7c9946074ec445e6d49ac42a6914ce82afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\ldots,9&lt;11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides none of the factors. Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf0761444de8298b30a7ccc51a3900417b2c496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\nmid1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdots9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the smallest positive integer that does not divide the product is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd34aa5e4f49c065b66db919bf81d6d611bc2bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of four-digit odd numbers having digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56018d4175e560429ba86a10b8d6931509ef820f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, each occuring exactly once, is:\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the number must be odd, its units digit must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the units digit.\n</p><p>After fixing the units digit, the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways for the thousands, hundreds, and tens places, respectively.\n</p><p>By the Fundamental Principle of Counting, the total number of ways is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8138e3a1a21440da11b2f89468523587af8cb42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot3\\cdot2\\cdot1=3!\\cdot2=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"181\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/38693a75a9e00c962455566cda9d06d94da1738b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number obtained by taking the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b6052613b91e6aae2b87f34da6f384cb62aaf221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> in the same order is:\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab660081d421ba9ad93273259efac9a7e27639a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369aa2b96d08192baf66da44577be596a58d6778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e4d230e75b3cb7fea5c98643fef4b6e775aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cc646ca0c60782ea5156c32bd6e1d7fa4bf92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}=5\\cdot5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c153188799ff6bcc201daa9796379d2b6b81f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n=100k+25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e23ede3810948562c012a8f2292386472d80288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}=5(100k+25)=500k+125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p>which ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, by mathematical induction, every power <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e4d230e75b3cb7fea5c98643fef4b6e775aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf46f6dc1582c17836a62d3b5104369fe36f50d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b6052613b91e6aae2b87f34da6f384cb62aaf221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> ends in\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d000f4c985761c51268403c667b77a77667f3339.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f5b43f0f50329adb2c9b7de02545601cdae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee59c4178aee21593add2c16b94aadcec762e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{x}{z}+\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{z}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/79378636e4aaff19079ef084e2aa59476d063a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}\\right)\\left(\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{z}{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"265\" height=\"45\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220eb8e9be877f81b85e73b2dc55e71fa4160833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|ab-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> is:\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f5b43f0f50329adb2c9b7de02545601cdae87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee59c4178aee21593add2c16b94aadcec762e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{x}{z}+\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{z}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" /> and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/79378636e4aaff19079ef084e2aa59476d063a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}\\right)\\left(\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{z}{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"265\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220eb8e9be877f81b85e73b2dc55e71fa4160833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|ab-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff13ae6e0c151383793124396cd90268ce7cf1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}\\right) \\left(\\frac{x}{z}+\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{z}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"272\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/99908054030eb1df28c598ba27b9696e3c999dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{x^2}{yz}+\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{xz}{y^2} +\\frac{xy}{z^2}+\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{y^2}{xz} +\\frac{z^2}{xy}+\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{yz}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"379\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef045e0b8f7c9b8d5d6905d63b746f7cd25e51d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{x^2}{yz}+\\frac{xz}{y^2}+\\frac{xy}{z^2} +\\frac{y^2}{xz}+\\frac{z^2}{xy}+\\frac{yz}{x^2}+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"304\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Also,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1e409e76a2d0b5c0deb39bd1c113c7a58e2870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{z}\\right) \\left(\\frac{y}{z}+\\frac{z}{x}\\right) \\left(\\frac{z}{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"265\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/33020249bd5f8cf09c020d01b040146bd50f4c40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\left(\\frac{xy}{yz}+\\frac{xz}{xy}+\\frac{y^2}{z^2}+\\frac{yz}{xz}\\right) \\left(\\frac{z}{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"287\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0aefe755462a66461752435b73fced530a9d915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\left(\\frac{x}{z}+\\frac{z}{y}+\\frac{y^2}{z^2}+\\frac{y}{x}\\right) \\left(\\frac{z}{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"257\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Expanding,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185ff58b99446b18b57f801f1420d5a71d48aab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{xy}{z x}+\\frac{x^2}{yz} +\\frac{z^2}{xy}+\\frac{xz}{y^2} +\\frac{y^2}{zx}+\\frac{y^2}{z^2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{y} +\\frac{yz}{x^2}+\\frac{1}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"392\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04917a3222eb064de29799705f6ad3e2a1b9116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{x^2}{yz}+\\frac{xz}{y^2}+\\frac{xy}{z^2} +\\frac{y^2}{xz}+\\frac{z^2}{xy}+\\frac{yz}{x^2}+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"317\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6cb04b6978b956d342e65e0bb395ac4d3021d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab-c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/445b8ab0cb458413d16ce83da7efffbd24ebd9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{|ab-c|=1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"104\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of triples of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711634e30233f3369dcc2f71f28f8aaabdeb065a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{20}+b^{20}+c^{20}=a^{24}+b^{24}+c^{24}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are even, replacing any of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> by its negative does not change either equation. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution iff changing the sign of any of its nonzero coordinates gives another solution.\n</p><p>First consider only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95d64884c3a200764fddaee1f7840c3b7061cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c92e017e6611d2f3f4069bb3e2c07b757ba1235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{20}+b^{20}+c^{20}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d32354db54ece24744d86355c02e5ff6aaa87f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a,b,c\\leq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc85d577fe000dadcf754da939788b1c001a97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq x\\leq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4722965dd6ea5890ae352c0a678aeefe1ead42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{24}\\leq x^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p><p>with equality only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b1f71d4dde986f934dbaf202191859e405c19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{24}+b^{24}+c^{24}\\leq a^{20}+b^{20}+c^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p><p>and equality is possible only if\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57d7be5c6f82e4fa74753fa46c0beab345a201f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c\\in\\{0,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c92e017e6611d2f3f4069bb3e2c07b757ba1235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{20}+b^{20}+c^{20}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>exactly one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other two are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the nonnegative solutions are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea99d85e88854143ce7c527958298b42115426ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0,0),\\quad(0,1,0),\\quad(0,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>For each solution, the nonzero coordinate can independently be replaced by its negative. Therefore the solutions are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805fdd082d9efa4cdac3e19a3a3dba8e5492435e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm1,0,0),\\quad(0,\\pm1,0),\\quad(0,0,\\pm1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the number of triples is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb760a2c7143780db481b394ada34e0bb23b3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the sum of all possible surface areas of a cube two of whose vertices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c0ee07c8aa7c0afb5fc92813ba4ddf68704f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e804b07a6641177cd5bf44a4d7af79b1192d509e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the two given vertices be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f11353a53479f0fb133e70c74f683abf0860f6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(1,2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059ccdd79e29741950b216ad5ba6dc4b6747b48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(3,3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d831bfffec0b5dfa018e26c9b07054b1be2a76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=\\sqrt{(3-1)^2+(3-2)^2+(2-0)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"303\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b1ba3a3040636f3c6e61db2872c65a021de62d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{4+1+4}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>There are three cases.\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is an edge.\n</p><p>Then the side length is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4955f631984fec9540e6bcb3c372e92c60d2da94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=3$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the surface area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b131bbe67c202f2ac9ba3698c8a6ca7c5667429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6s^2=6(9)=54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diagonal of a face.\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8dc6c7af1a201311ae89db52074e0a5a31d00af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\sqrt{2}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/1020f240ed2ae891146e73d2725acfeeec7f0c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2=\\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the surface area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5b32b68e84931937db84c085bd7696b8d9b413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6s^2=6\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)=27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"145\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 3:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a space diagonal.\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feeb6a68f48a802dbf23373497878ede48d8de42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\sqrt{3}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a67bb94cf9e5de920f7d560787bf20e22e89df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the surface area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9456696e3119f4e44e3a94473994b2b72ae60c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6s^2=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the required sum is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b2955e6666f72addd1bd573afb2b2f721e606f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54+27+18=\\boxed{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest integer such that the sum of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as well as the sum of\ndigits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/34955dfb34e090d3051cd8c656604d79915aef93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What are the first two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in the same order?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0da9d41b0b691daa995e2262b62bb3b7490726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy the folowing equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f3f3d02a8b7f6e62796b08f50a7e38f1464630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac + b + c = bc + a + 66, a + b + c = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />.\nFind the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, you are allowed two operations: (1) multiply by 2 or (2) subtract 3 from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. For example starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> you can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/23878ad3a2f132b8d4cc0a6bd9b13a7068faa303.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\rightarrow 16\\rightarrow 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />.You need two steps and you cannot do in less than two steps. Starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the least number of steps required to reach 121&#160;?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=29\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=30\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_26\">Problem 26</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 26\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_27\">Problem 27</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 27\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_28\">Problem 28</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=34\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 28\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_29\">Problem 29</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=35\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 29\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_30\">Problem 30</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IOQM_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=36\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 30\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065914\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 697/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22373/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!